# ADR-003: Use GitOps for Kubernetes delivery

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-08-23

## Context

The project is intended to demonstrate safe, auditable delivery. A pipeline that has privileged access to a Kubernetes cluster mixes build and deployment concerns and provides weak visibility into deployed desired state.

## Decision

GitHub Actions will validate, test, and build application artifacts. It will not apply workloads directly to Kubernetes. A reviewed change in the `platform-gitops` repository will define the desired deployment version. Argo CD will reconcile that repository with the cluster.

## Consequences

- The cluster's intended state is reviewable in version control.
- CI permissions can be narrower than direct cluster-administration permissions.
- Delivery requires an additional repository update, which is deliberate evidence of promotion control.
- Argo CD availability becomes part of the delivery path and must be monitored.
